        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T04:18:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Using `WillOnce` makes this a very fragile mock. Instead, I think we need to do the following:\n\nUse `ON_CALL` to point to a default response that returns default values for all the supported/expected commands.\n\nUse a custom matcher that lets you identify a specific UCSI command to respond to.\nUse another custom matcher that is a combination of UCSI command + port.\n\nFor example:\n\n```\n  ON_CALL(*pd_driver_mock_, ExecuteCmd).WillByDefault(ReturnDefaultValuesForCmds);\n  \n  ON_CALL(*pd_driver_mock, ExecuteCmd(_, CommandMatches(UCSI_CMD_GET_PDO), _))\n     .WillOnce(Invoke(\u0026kGetPdoUniqueRsp, fptr));\n     \n  ON_CALL(*pd_driver_mock, \n    ExecuteCmd(_, CommandPortMatches(UCSI_CMD_GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS, 1))\n    .WillByDefault(Invoke(\u0026kConnectorStatusOn1, fptr));\n```\n\nWe want to validate that providing a certain response to various UCSI commands result in the correct changes in OPM / sysfs and not strictly care about what does get called.\n\nIn case, we DO care and want to enforce it, we can still use `EXPECT_CALL(...).Times(N)` to enforce it using the matchers described above.",
      "revId": "288abfa2ee6b8970147181b6eb92b789fbf9dc22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99a44739_f42e4ee3",
        "filename": "extra/um_ppm/test/opm_tests.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 651,
      "author": {
        "id": 1498599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T12:00:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right that current strict use of WillOnce causes the unit tests to be not stable. I agree that order and number of calls is not so important as the result (sysfs entries). I will use ON_CALL where it is possible.\nBut I will need to also use EXPECT_CALL for example for get connector status because the get connector status message is the same each but the replies differ.",
      "parentUuid": "5eea6363_91236406",
      "revId": "288abfa2ee6b8970147181b6eb92b789fbf9dc22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "01318c20_300752cd",
        "filename": "extra/um_ppm/test/opm_tests.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 651,
      "author": {
        "id": 1365249
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T15:37:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure but those EXPECT_CALL should be in-line with other things being called in your test.\n\ni.e.\n\n```\nconstexpr int kDefaultPort \u003d 1;\n\nTEST_F(Foo, Bar) {\n  SetupMock();\n  \n  // Trigger a partner connected event. Should result in connector status check\n  // at least twice.\n  EXPECT_CALL(*pd_driver_mock_, \n    ExecuteCmd(_, CommandPortMatches(UCSI_CMD_GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS, kDefaultPort))\n    .WillRepeatedly(Invoke(\u0026kConstatPartnerChange, fptr));\n    .Times(Ge(2));\n    \n  ppm_drv-\u003elpm_alert(ppm_drv-\u003edev, kDefaultPort);\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "99a44739_f42e4ee3",
      "revId": "288abfa2ee6b8970147181b6eb92b789fbf9dc22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7fd73ab1_cf18f1d6",
        "filename": "extra/um_ppm/test/opm_tests.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 651,
      "author": {
        "id": 1498599
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-22T16:05:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes but rather something like \n```\n  EXPECT_CALL(*pd_driver_mock_, \n    ExecuteCmd(_, CommandPortMatches(UCSI_CMD_GET_CONNECTOR_STATUS,kDefaultPort))\n       .WillOnce(Invoke(\u0026kPartnerUpdate1, fptr));\n       .WillOnce(Invoke(\u0026kPartnerUpdate2, fptr));\n       .WillOnce(Invoke(\u0026kPartnerUpdate3, fptr));\n       .WillRepeatedly(Invoke(\u0026kPartnerUpdateFinal, fptr));\n       .Times(Ge(4));\n```\nbecause get connector status message is the same each time and the replies change.",
      "parentUuid": "01318c20_300752cd",
      "revId": "288abfa2ee6b8970147181b6eb92b789fbf9dc22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
