      "message": "Actually mixing ON_CALL with EXPECT_CALL is not very good idea because EXPECT_CALL has precedence which ends with an error for example:\n```\n\nunknown file: Failure\n\nUnexpected mock function call - taking default action specified at:\nopm_tests.cc:785:\n    Function call: execute_cmd(0x5ce40125d3a0, 0x5ce40125d592, 0x5ce40125d59a)\n          Returns: 0\nGoogle Mock tried the following 25 expectations, but none matched:\n```\n\nON_CALL\u0027s default action was executed from line 785:\n```\n        ON_CALL(*_pdDriverMock, execute_cmd(_,\n                MatchCmd(UCSI_CMD_PPM_RESET), _))\n                .WillByDefault(Invoke(\u0026ppm_reset, fptr));\n```\n\nBut even though test was declared as failed.\nBased on that I will stick only to EXPECT_CALL.",
